---
description: UI copy must be English-only (no Cyrillic in user-facing strings)
globs: app/**/*.{tsx,ts},lib/**/*.{tsx,ts}
alwaysApply: false
---

# UI language: English only

All user-visible copy in `app/` and `lib/` must be English — labels, buttons, toasts, footnotes, empty states, agent text.

## Allowed non-ASCII

Currency symbols (₽, $), arrows (→), math (≈, −, +) are fine.

## Not allowed in UI strings

Cyrillic in JSX text, button labels, hints, or lib strings returned to the UI.

Regex/parsers matching Russian bank exports may keep Cyrillic in patterns — not shown to users.

## Check before merge

```bash
grep -rnP '[\x{0400}-\x{04FF}]' app lib --include='*.tsx' --include='*.ts' | grep -v '\.test\.' | grep -vE 'match:|test\(|/[^/]+/[i]*'
```

Fix any hits that are user-facing; update tests if copy changes.
